# Architecture Rules

## Project Structure

Feature-based architecture: each feature (steam, voice, poll, admin, general, community) is self-contained under `src/features/`.

- `src/features/` — Feature modules, each with commands/, services/, events/, and index.ts
  - `src/features/steam/` — Steam integration (commands incl. /server stats, steam client, notifications, scheduler)
  - `src/features/voice/` — Voice recording (commands, connection manager, audio buffer, events)
  - `src/features/poll/` — Poll system (commands, poll store/service)
  - `src/features/admin/` — Admin commands (admin, settings)
  - `src/features/general/` — General commands (ping, help)
  - `src/features/community/` — Community commands (roulette)
- `src/events/` — Core event handlers (ready, interactionCreate)
- `src/services/` — Shared services (database, backup, health, metrics, cooldown, audit)
- `src/handlers/` — Command/event loading from both features/*/commands/ and features/*/events/
- `src/middleware/` — Pre-execution checks (cooldown, permissions, etc.)
- `src/utils/` — Pure utilities (logger, embed builder, chart, retry, etc.)
- `src/config/` — Environment config, validation, and constants
- `src/types/` — TypeScript type definitions
- `src/locales/` — i18n translations (en, ja)
- `src/scripts/` — Utility scripts (e.g., cleanup-commands)
- `src/__tests__/` — Unit and integration tests (vitest)

## Coding Standards

### Error Handling

- Always wrap command/event execution in try-catch
- Log errors with `logger.error()` — never use empty catch blocks
- Use `error instanceof Error ? error.message : error` pattern for safe logging
- Commands should reply with user-friendly error embeds, not raw error messages
- Use `process.on('unhandledRejection')` and `process.on('uncaughtException')` at the top level

### Database

- Use prepared statements for all queries (already enforced by better-sqlite3)
- Use `runTransaction()` for operations that modify multiple tables
- Table names in dynamic queries must be validated against `ALLOWED_TABLES`
- All table creation should be inside `initializeDatabase()` within a transaction

### Voice

- Use the `entersState` + `Promise.race` pattern from `@discordjs/voice` for disconnect handling
- Always clean up audio buffers when disconnecting (`audioBufferManager.removeBuffer`)
- Respect `MAX_CONCURRENT_VC_CONNECTIONS` limit

### Services & Features

- Follow singleton pattern for service instances (export `const instance = new Service()`)
- Each feature module exports `start(client)` / `stop()` in its `index.ts`
- Register feature lifecycle in `src/index.ts` and handle cleanup in `gracefulShutdown()`
- Start features that depend on Discord after `client.login()`
- New features go in `src/features/<name>/` with `commands/`, `services/`, and optionally `events/`

### Localization

- Use `t(locale, key, ...args)` for user-facing text
- Map Discord locales with `mapDiscordLocale(interaction.locale)`
- Add translations to both `en.ts` and `ja.ts`

### Testing

- Test files go in `src/__tests__/` mirroring the source structure
- Use vitest for all tests; mock Discord.js objects and external services
- Integration tests in `src/__tests__/integration/`
- Use `vi.mock()` at the top of test files for module mocking
- Prefer async/await tests; all service methods that return promises should be awaited in tests

### File I/O

- Prefer `fs/promises` (async) over `fs` sync methods in async contexts
- Use `createWriteStream` for large file writes
- Sync methods (`existsSync`, `mkdirSync`) are acceptable only in constructors and module-level initialization
